From e7ce5eb4cf8514b3314c973dc6fa8c6c87c5145c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <services.claude@accounts.ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 18:37:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: Phase 11 patch 0070 -- v2 Pixtone probe pix_active
 histogram + irq_delta fold-in

Why DOS needs this:

The v1 Pixtone multi-source probe iter (nxengine-evo/0165, 2026-05-20)
returned hypothesis-E (instrumentation gap) per
docs/internal/486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md sec.21.5. Root cause: the
v1 engine-side histogram sampler (SamplePixtoneActiveBucket at
Renderer.cpp) was hooked to organyaStreamCallback, which fires only
under the Organya music backend. OPL3 has been the wave-46 default
since 2026-05-14, so the sampler never fired in the production
configuration -> samples=0 across all 13 v1 probe blocks ->
discriminator-pillar table unable to compute hypotheses A vs C.

This patch re-wires the histogram sampling to the SDL-side audio
backend: g_pixtone_active_count is sampled once per audio-thread
iterate (top of DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice), bucketed into the same 6
bins as the v1 engine-side histogram ([0] / [1] / [2] / [3-5] /
[6-10] / [11+] -- boundaries match Renderer.cpp:122). PlayDevice is
the unified-cadence point that fires regardless of music backend
(Organya / OPL3 / WaveBlaster all funnel through SDL3_mixer ->
PlayDevice). Hypothesis-E instrumentation gap closes.

Secondary resolution -- v1 sec.21.4.1 silent_irq numeric anomaly:

The v1 iter also surfaced an arithmetic anomaly: silent_irq delta
~750 per 100-flip block. Design-assumed 43 Hz IRQ rate predicts
~190 IRQs/block over a 4.4-second block -- so silent_irq is 4x the
total IRQ count, which is impossible (silent_irq counts a subset of
total IRQs). Source-verified investigation #116 cleared the SDL/0069
wiring (single increment per silent IRQ; engine-side delta arithmetic
correct), leaving the IRQ rate hypothesis: real DX2-66 SB16 may fire
IRQ-5 at a higher rate than the design assumption.

This patch folds the existing doskutsu_audio_irq_count delta into the
same [sdl-audiocb] block emit as `irq_delta=N`. The existing counter
already increments unconditionally per IRQ at sb.c:778; no new symbol
needed (per #117 STOP-and-ack Q2 narrowing -- pre-flight grep caught
the existing counter). The block-emit delta exposes the real-HW IRQ
rate as a per-block witness, resolving the sec.21.4.1 anomaly.
Snapshot pattern matches Renderer.cpp:3157 (modular wrap-safe per
C99 unsigned overflow semantics).

Patch shape:

  - extern volatile uint32_t g_pixtone_active_count -- engine -> SDL
    extern direction. Novel for this codebase but linkage-clean: the
    engine-side symbol is in an extern "C" block at Pixtone.h:37.
  - static Uint32 g_c_pix_hist[6] -- file-scope histogram, touched
    only from the cooperative audio thread (PlayDevice + record).
    No DPMI lock needed -- never read or written from IRQ context.
  - static Uint32 g_c_audiocb_last_irq_count -- previous-block-emit
    snapshot for irq_count delta computation.
  - _c_pix_hist_sample helper: single volatile read + branched
    bucket-inc, negligible cost.
  - PlayDevice top-of-body sample call, gated on the existing
    g_c_sfx_audiocb_instr_active cached bool (FINE_INSTR=1 from
    SDL/0064). No new env var; rides on the existing gate.
  - _c_audiocb_record extends the existing [sdl-audiocb] emit with
    `pix_active min=X med=Y p90=Z max=W samples=N irq_delta=M` fields.
    Per-100-PlayDevice-call cadence unchanged. Histogram + irq snapshot
    reset on emit alongside the existing reset block.
  - OpenDevice banner: "audio: SDL/0070 v2 Pixtone probe pix_active
    histogram + irq_delta fold-in: rides on FINE_INSTR=1" -- the
    smoke gate's runtime-invocation witness; banner is unconditional
    so embed-vs-runtime is observable.

Total: 135 lines in vendor/SDL/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
(comment density per the file's existing convention). Zero new env
var. Zero new counter symbol. Zero engine LOC. Zero new patches for
the Lever 4 ride-along (PLAY2 sets existing DEVICE_FRAMES + RING_CHUNKS
env vars per #115 design).

Banner regex added to tests/run-gameplay-smoke.sh BANNERS array;
parity 46 -> 47 across BANNER_REGEX / BANNER_SEVERITY / BANNER_LABEL.

Workspace-local per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md; never upstreamed.

See docs/internal/PIXTONE-PROBE-V2-DESIGN.md sec.2 + sec.5 for the
contract this patch implements + #117 STOP-and-ack closure (Q2
narrowing accepted).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 137 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 135 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 0d11dafec..d37139cfa 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -205,2 +205,44 @@ static Uint32 g_c_audiocb_block = 0;       /* emitted-block counter */
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0070): v2 Pixtone multi-source probe.
+   Sibling of nxengine 0165's engine-side histogram at
+   `vendor/nxengine-evo/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp:129` (g_pix_hist_bucket).
+   The v1 engine-side site (SamplePixtoneActiveBucket called from
+   organyaStreamCallback) fires only under the Organya backend, which
+   produced hypothesis-E in the v1 probe iter because OPL3 has been the
+   wave-46 default since 2026-05-14. This SDL-side site samples at the
+   top of DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice -- the unified-cadence point that
+   fires regardless of music backend (Organya / OPL3 / WaveBlaster all
+   funnel through SDL3_mixer -> SB16 device path).
+
+   Bucket boundaries match nxengine 0165 (Renderer.cpp:122): [0] / [1]
+   / [2] / [3-5] / [6-10] / [11+]. Sampling rate = once per audio-thread
+   iterate (one PlayDevice call). Cross-comparable with the v1 engine-
+   side histogram if both engage in a Tier-1 / Organya cell.
+
+   Gate: rides on the existing FINE_INSTR=1 cached bool from patch
+   SDL/0064 (g_c_sfx_audiocb_instr_active). No new env var, no new
+   cached-bool. FINE_INSTR=0 cost is one cached-bool test (already paid).
+
+   Storage: file-scope static array (no DPMI lock needed -- touched
+   only from the cooperative audio thread, never from IRQ context;
+   matches the existing g_c_audiocb_* counter pattern).
+
+   Per docs/internal/PIXTONE-PROBE-V2-DESIGN.md sec.2 + flush-instr's
+   #117 contract review. */
+extern volatile uint32_t g_pixtone_active_count; /* engine -> SDL extern */
+static Uint32 g_c_pix_hist[6] = {0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0};
+
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0070): irq_count delta fold-in.
+   Snapshot of doskutsu_audio_irq_count at the previous block emit;
+   current block's delta `irq_delta` exposes the real-HW SB16 IRQ-5
+   firing rate as a per-block witness. Sibling of silent_irq delta
+   (engine reads doskutsu_audio_silent_irq_count via patch 0069). The
+   ratio silent_irq / irq_delta gives the silent fraction; irq_delta
+   per wall-second gives the actual IRQ rate. Resolves the v1 sec.21.4.1
+   anomaly (silent_irq ~750/block vs design-assumed 43 Hz IRQ predicting
+   ~190 IRQs/block over 4.4 s). Snapshot-pattern matches the engine-side
+   reader at `vendor/nxengine-evo/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp:3157`.
+   Modular wrap-safe per C99 unsigned overflow semantics. */
+static Uint32 g_c_audiocb_last_irq_count = 0;
+
 /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0066): audio-thread hard-park
@@ -1063,2 +1105,14 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
 
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0070): banner for the v2 Pixtone
+       probe re-wire. The pix_active histogram + irq_delta fold-in
+       engage when FINE_INSTR=1 turns on the [sdl-audiocb] block emit
+       gate (see SDL/0064 banner above for the FINE_INSTR variant).
+       Resolves the v1 probe hypothesis-E instrumentation gap (nxengine
+       0165's organyaStreamCallback sampler missed the OPL3 default
+       since wave-46). Pure-data instrumentation; no behavior change.
+       Per docs/internal/PIXTONE-PROBE-V2-DESIGN.md sec.2 + sec.5. */
+    doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0070 v2 Pixtone probe pix_active histogram "
+                     "+ irq_delta fold-in: rides on FINE_INSTR=1 (extends "
+                     "[sdl-audiocb] block emit; no new env var)");
+
     /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0050): resolve quiescence-gate
@@ -1950,2 +2004,21 @@ static Uint8 *DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf(SDL_AudioDevice *device, int *buffer_
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0070): bucket the current
+   g_pixtone_active_count into the 6-bucket histogram. Boundaries match
+   nxengine 0165 (Renderer.cpp:122): [0] / [1] / [2] / [3-5] / [6-10] /
+   [11+]. Called from the top of DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice under
+   FINE_INSTR=1; one single-volatile-read + one branched bucket-inc;
+   negligible cost. */
+static void _c_pix_hist_sample(void)
+{
+    const Uint32 n = g_pixtone_active_count;
+    int b;
+    if (n == 0)       b = 0;
+    else if (n == 1)  b = 1;
+    else if (n == 2)  b = 2;
+    else if (n <= 5)  b = 3;
+    else if (n <= 10) b = 4;
+    else              b = 5;
+    g_c_pix_hist[b]++;
+}
+
 /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0064): close one SDL-DOS audio-
@@ -1978,4 +2051,46 @@ static void _c_audiocb_record(void)
         g_c_audiocb_block++;
+
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0070): compute pix_active
+           percentiles (min / med / p90 / max) from the 6-bucket
+           histogram. Bucket midpoints match nxengine 0165 design
+           for cross-comparison: 0 / 1 / 2 / 4 / 8 / 12. Cumulative
+           threshold scan; coarse but sufficient at probe resolution. */
+        static const Uint32 _bucket_mid[6] = {0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 12};
+        Uint32 _pix_total = 0;
+        for (int i = 0; i < 6; ++i) _pix_total += g_c_pix_hist[i];
+        Uint32 _pix_min = 0, _pix_med = 0, _pix_p90 = 0, _pix_max = 0;
+        if (_pix_total > 0) {
+            for (int i = 0; i < 6; ++i) {
+                if (g_c_pix_hist[i]) { _pix_min = _bucket_mid[i]; break; }
+            }
+            for (int i = 5; i >= 0; --i) {
+                if (g_c_pix_hist[i]) { _pix_max = _bucket_mid[i]; break; }
+            }
+            const Uint32 _thr_med = _pix_total / 2;
+            const Uint32 _thr_p90 = (_pix_total * 90) / 100;
+            Uint32 _acc = 0;
+            int _set_med = 0, _set_p90 = 0;
+            for (int i = 0; i < 6; ++i) {
+                _acc += g_c_pix_hist[i];
+                if (!_set_med && _acc >= _thr_med) {
+                    _pix_med = _bucket_mid[i]; _set_med = 1;
+                }
+                if (!_set_p90 && _acc >= _thr_p90) {
+                    _pix_p90 = _bucket_mid[i]; _set_p90 = 1;
+                }
+            }
+        }
+
+        /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0070): irq_count delta vs the
+           previous block-emit snapshot. The witness for real-HW IRQ
+           rate (sec.21.4.1 anomaly resolver). Modular wrap-safe per
+           C99 unsigned overflow semantics. */
+        const Uint32 _now_irq = doskutsu_audio_irq_count;
+        const Uint32 _d_irq = _now_irq - g_c_audiocb_last_irq_count;
+        g_c_audiocb_last_irq_count = _now_irq;
+
         doskutsu_dbg_log("[sdl-audiocb block~%lu invocations=%lu "
-                         "total_ms=%lu max_ms=%lu]",
+                         "total_ms=%lu max_ms=%lu "
+                         "pix_active min=%lu med=%lu p90=%lu max=%lu "
+                         "samples=%lu irq_delta=%lu]",
                          (unsigned long)g_c_audiocb_block,
@@ -1983,3 +2098,9 @@ static void _c_audiocb_record(void)
                          (unsigned long)(g_c_audiocb_total_ns / 1000000ULL),
-                         (unsigned long)(g_c_audiocb_max_ns / 1000000ULL));
+                         (unsigned long)(g_c_audiocb_max_ns / 1000000ULL),
+                         (unsigned long)_pix_min,
+                         (unsigned long)_pix_med,
+                         (unsigned long)_pix_p90,
+                         (unsigned long)_pix_max,
+                         (unsigned long)_pix_total,
+                         (unsigned long)_d_irq);
         g_c_audiocb_invocations = 0;
@@ -1987,2 +2108,3 @@ static void _c_audiocb_record(void)
         g_c_audiocb_max_ns = 0;
+        for (int i = 0; i < 6; ++i) g_c_pix_hist[i] = 0;
     }
@@ -1996,2 +2118,13 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device, const Uint8 *buf
 
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0070): v2 Pixtone probe -- sample
+       g_pixtone_active_count once per PlayDevice invocation (= once per
+       audio-thread iterate). Buckets into g_c_pix_hist[6] for the
+       per-block emit in _c_audiocb_record. PlayDevice fires regardless
+       of music backend -- closes the v1 hypothesis-E instrumentation
+       gap (Organya-only sampler missed the OPL3 default since wave-46).
+       Cached-bool gate; FINE_INSTR=0 cost is the one test. */
+    if (g_c_sfx_audiocb_instr_active) {
+        _c_pix_hist_sample();
+    }
+
     /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0055): P12 SDL-side audio bracket
-- 
